{"url": "https://www.sdstate.edu/mathematics-statistics/graduate-mathematics-statistics-programs", "final_url": "https://www.sdstate.edu/mathematics-statistics/graduate-mathematics-statistics-programs", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-28", "text": "Graduate Mathematics and Statistics Programs | South Dakota State University\nSkip to main content\nApply\nVisit\nDirectories\nDegree Finder\nFaculty and Staff\nOffice Directory\nBuildings Directory\nEvent Calendar\nCampus Map\nSDSTATE\nSearch\nVisit\nDegree Finder\nCampus Map\nSDSTATE\nSearch\nFilter by Topic\nBlog Event News Profile Program\nClose Search Box\nsection-mathematics-and-statisti\nResearch\nBioinformatics Research Group\nSDSU Statistical Consulting Center\nCAPITAL Services Statistical Learning Scholar\nPrograms\nUndergraduate Programs\nGraduate Programs\nOnline Courses and Programs\nUndergraduate Courses\nMath Placement\nHigh School Dual Credit\nStudents\nMath Help Center\nMathematics Supplemental Labs\nJacks LeaP for Math Success\nWho Hires Grads?\nEvents\nSummer Data Science Camp\nSDSU Data Science Symposium\nApply\nGraduate Programs\nUndergraduate Programs\nWork at SDSU\nGraduate Assistantships\nMath Help Center Tutors\nOur People\nSearch\nApply Today\nSDSTATE\nBreadcrumb\n...\nHome\nDepartment of Mathematics and Statistics\nPrograms\nGraduate Mathematics and Statistics Programs\nFollow Us:\nInstagram\nLinkedin\nFacebook\nEmail\n605-688-6196\nDriving the Decisions That Shape Our World\nMathematics, statistics and data science play key roles in helping us understand and make decisions to improve every part of our society.\nGraduate Admissions\nGraduate Programs\nAll four programs offer students the opportunity to pursue graduate studies in a collegial environment with high faculty-student interaction and research activity, and are particularly effective at preparing graduates to work in business, industry or government as well as the more traditional area of higher education.\nMathematics (M.S.)\nStatistics (M.S.)\nData Science (M.S.)\nComputational Science and Statistics (Ph.D.)\nGet More\nAccelerated Masters Degrees\nSDSU undergraduate mathematics and data science majors may take 12 credits of graduate mathematics and statistics courses during their senior year, and count these credits towards both their bachelor\u2019s and master\u2019s degrees. The remaining credits needed to obtain the master\u2019s then fit comfortably into one additional year of study.\nM.S. in mathematics\nM.S. in statistics\nM.S. in data science\nopportunity\nGraduate Assistantships\nAssistantships are available on a competitive basis.\nMany graduate research and teaching assistantships and fellowships are available (currently 38), though applicants should note that admission to the graduate program does not guarantee that an assistantship or fellowship will be awarded.\nGraduate Assistantships Opportunities\nApplication for Admission\nLink to Graduate Admission Requirements\nRequirements\nApplications may be submitted at any time, but it is recommended that applications for admission for the fall semester be made by Feb. 15 for master's degree programs and by Dec. 15 for the Ph.D. program. Application and graduate assistantship decisions are generally made by the first week of March. Late applications will be considered for both admission and assistantships, but assistantship availability for such applications is likely to be reduced.\nGraduate Admission Requirements\nLink to Graduate Admissions\nGraduate Application\nAt the department level, admission decisions are based on applicants' level of achievement in prerequisite undergraduate courses and the extent to which applicants' educational and professional goals align with the department's areas of specialization.GRE scores are not required or considered.\nGraduate Admissions\nGraduate Program Resources\nUseful tools as you evaluate our graduate programs.\nCourse Rotation\nResearch\nContact Information\nDonald Vestal\nAssociate Professor/Coordinator\nEmail\n605-688-4856 for Donald Vestal\nDepartment of Mathematics and Statistics\nPhysical Address\n905 Campanile Ave.\nBrookings,\nSD\n57007\nMailing Address\nSAME 276, Box 2225\nBrookings,\nSD\n57007\nView Location\nHours\nMon - Fri:\n8:00 a.m.-5:00 p.m.\nEmail\n605-688-6196\nFollow Us\nFacebook\nInstagram\nLinkedin\nVisit Us\nCome Meet Your Future\nMeet the people that will help shape your future and define your college experience! Learn more about your academic interests with some of our world-class faculty.\nApply Today\nPlan Your Visit\nRequest Info\nResearch\nPrograms\nStudents\nEvents\nApply\nOur People\nGet Directions\nGive to SDSU\nOffice Directory\nExplore\nAbout SDState\nAcademics\nAdmissions\nStudent Life\nResearch\nCommunity\nConnect\nAlumni\nAthletics\nBookstore\nEvent Calendar\nGiving\nLibrary\nNews\nFor Students\nD2L\nJacks Club Hub\nJacks Email\nMyJacks Card\nMyState\nSelf Service\nFor Faculty and Staff\nEmployment\nFaculty and Staff Directory\nInsideState\nMy Account\n\u00a9 2026 All Rights Reserved.\nEmergency\nEAO\nLegal\nMission\nPolicies\nReport It\nSDState Facebook\nSDState X.com\nSDState Youtube\nSDState Instagram\nSDState LinkedIn\nSearch\nFilter by Topic\nBlog Event News Profile Program\nsection-mathematics-and-statisti\nResearch\nBioinformatics Research Group\nSDSU Statistical Consulting Center\nCAPITAL Services Statistical Learning Scholar\nPrograms\nUndergraduate Programs\nGraduate Programs\nOnline Courses and Programs\nUndergraduate Courses\nMath Placement\nHigh School Dual Credit\nStudents\nMath Help Center\nMathematics Supplemental Labs\nJacks LeaP for Math Success\nWho Hires Grads?\nEvents\nSummer Data Science Camp\nSDSU Data Science Symposium\nApply\nGraduate Programs\nUndergraduate Programs\nWork at SDSU\nGraduate Assistantships\nMath Help Center Tutors\nOur People\nSearch\nApply Today\nSDSTATE\nApply\nVisit\nDirectories\nDegree Finder\nFaculty and Staff\nOffice Directory\nBuildings Directory\nEven